    {
      "title": "News live: Albanese hits back at Hanson criticism of his mother’s use of public housing; Melissa Doyle appointed Australia Day council chair",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/13/australia-news-live-chris-bowen-middle-east-fuel-petrol-prices-anika-wells-social-media-algorithm-andrew-hastie-pauline-hanson-one-nation-albanese-labor-coalition-liberal-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow today’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Andrew Hastie</strong> says he “feels sorry” for <strong>Barnaby Joyce</strong> and that he and One Nation MP <strong>David Farley</strong> probably have “buyers remorse” after joining the rightwing party.</p><p>Hastie has been feuding with <strong>Pauline Hanson</strong> this week over a One Nation animated cartoon which labelled him a “traitor” after he gave evidence against Ben Roberts-Smith in his failed defamation trial.</p><p>If she were to be prime minister, is she going to run cartoons about all her political opponents? How’s she going to devote her time? Is she serious? Does she have a worldview that we can actually understand? These are all legitimate questions for One Nation …</p><p>The whole party centres on her. <strong>I think this is why Barnaby Joyce and I reckon David Farley are probably having buyer’s remorse. They’re thinking, “what did I get myself into?</strong>”</p><p>Look, I’ll say this about Barnaby Joyce. I feel sorry for the bloke, all right? He left a party that made him deputy prime minister twice, to jump in with this rabble, there’s no principles, they’re all over the shop, and he’s out there every week cleaning up after them.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/13/australia-news-live-chris-bowen-middle-east-fuel-petrol-prices-anika-wells-social-media-algorithm-andrew-hastie-pauline-hanson-one-nation-albanese-labor-coalition-liberal-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-13T01:36:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "Andrew Hastie vows to go ‘all the way’ in Pauline Hanson fight as Joyce denies ‘buyers’ remorse’ claim",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/andrew-hastie-vows-to-go-all-the-way-in-fight-against-pauline-hanson-as-joyce-denies-buyers-remorse-claim-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Liberal MP says One Nation leader is ‘not the person I thought she was’ and he feels ‘sorry’ for Joyce</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/13/australia-news-live-chris-bowen-middle-east-fuel-petrol-prices-anika-wells-social-media-algorithm-andrew-hastie-pauline-hanson-one-nation-albanese-labor-coalition-liberal-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Andrew Hastie has vowed to go “all the way” in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/12/andrew-hastie-knew-attacking-pauline-hanson-would-cost-him-liberals-are-divided-over-the-price-of-following-suit-ntwnfb\">his fight with Pauline Hanson</a>, as he suggested One Nation MPs Barnaby Joyce and David Farley were likely feeling buyers’ remorse for joining the party.</p><p>The Liberal MP and former SAS captain repeated <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/11/andrew-hastie-accepts-joyce-apology-traitor-cartoon-hanson-tells-critics-chill-ntwnfb\">his accusation</a> that Hanson was a “lying coward” on Sunday, after she continued to refuse to take down an animated cartoon that described Hastie as a “traitor”. This came after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/11/andrew-hastie-reluctant-witness-ben-roberts-smith-case-one-nation-traitor-attack-ntwnfb\">he was subpoenaed to give evidence</a> during Ben Roberts-Smith’s failed defamation trial.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/andrew-hastie-vows-to-go-all-the-way-in-fight-against-pauline-hanson-as-joyce-denies-buyers-remorse-claim-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-13T01:34:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "Do not call her a racist: anti-Pauline Hanson strategists tell campaigners character attacks won’t work in Victoria",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/do-not-call-her-a-racist-anti-pauline-hanson-strategists-tell-campaigners-character-attacks-wont-work-in-victoria",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> strategic rethink urges progressive activists to respectfully steer one-on-one conversations with One Nation supporters towards economic concerns</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/13/australia-news-live-chris-bowen-middle-east-fuel-petrol-prices-anika-wells-social-media-algorithm-andrew-hastie-pauline-hanson-one-nation-albanese-labor-coalition-liberal-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The message from strategists was blunt: do not, however tempting, personally attack Pauline Hanson or call her a racist.</p><p>The request has been made to progressive campaigners and unionists who have been asked to start one-on-one conversations with One Nation supporters before the Victorian election in November.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/do-not-call-her-a-racist-anti-pauline-hanson-strategists-tell-campaigners-character-attacks-wont-work-in-victoria\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-12T20:00:45"
    },
